---
.title = "Environment Variables",
.date = "2026-10-01",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

In Zig, the standard process entry point `main(init: std.process.Init)` provides an already populated environment variable map via `init.environ_map` (an instance of `*std.process.Environ.Map`). Applications can directly query, inspect, set, or iterate environment variables without manual OS-level parsing.

Key operations:

- `env.get(key)`: Looks up an environment variable value, returning `null` if not present;
- `env.contains(key)`: Checks whether a variable exists in the environment map;
- `env.put(key, value)`: Inserts or updates an environment variable;
- `env.iterator()`: Returns an iterator over all key-value environment pairs;
- `env.orderedRemove(key)` or `env.swapRemove(key)`: Deletes an entry from the map.

